WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.390
A calendar shows when you’re busy. It rarely shows which promises depend

00:00:04.390 --> 00:00:08.780
on each other. For a student balancing exams, interviews, and club responsibilities,

00:00:08.780 --> 00:00:13.171
one changed date can break the whole week. Dira connects those commitments

00:00:13.171 --> 00:00:15.000
and helps repair the consequences.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:20.714
Here’s a synthetic student week. The professor moves Friday’s exam to Wednesday.

00:00:20.714 --> 00:00:26.429
That leaves too little preparation time, breaks the recovery buffer before an

00:00:26.429 --> 00:00:32.143
interview, and conflicts with club work. Dira’s feasibility engine exposes all three

00:00:32.143 --> 00:00:35.000
problems. Available slack drops below zero.

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:41.439
NVIDIA Nemotron Super, running on Nebius Token Factory, interprets the email. Ultra

00:00:41.439 --> 00:00:47.878
proposes structured repair candidates. Deterministic code checks their sources, feasibility, and policy

00:00:47.878 --> 00:00:54.317
before selecting a plan. This deliberately malicious candidate cites a nonexistent message.

00:00:54.317 --> 00:00:57.000
Dira rejects it before execution.

00:00:57.000 --> 00:01:03.486
The plan proposes rebooking the interview, moving flexible work, rebuilding study time,

00:01:03.486 --> 00:01:09.973
and delegating the club task. Delegation requires my approval. Dira pauses the

00:01:09.973 --> 00:01:16.459
entire plan here. The independent surface comparison confirms that nothing has changed

00:01:16.459 --> 00:01:17.000
yet.

00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:23.792
After I approve, Dira revalidates the plan against fresh state. The first

00:01:23.792 --> 00:01:30.585
interview slot is already taken. Rather than pretending it succeeded, Dira observes

00:01:30.585 --> 00:01:37.377
the failure and replans around another offered slot. Each action needs an

00:01:37.377 --> 00:01:44.170
independent read-back before the internal graph is updated. In this run, deterministic

00:01:44.170 --> 00:01:47.000
planning supplies the winning repair.

00:01:47.000 --> 00:01:52.217
Thirteen actions are verified, and slack returns to positive territory. Study time

00:01:52.217 --> 00:01:57.435
is restored before the exam, flexible work moves, and Maya becomes the

00:01:57.435 --> 00:02:02.652
task owner. The interview request remains explicitly marked as awaiting the counterparty.

00:02:02.652 --> 00:02:07.000
A successful request is never presented as someone else’s confirmation.

00:02:07.000 --> 00:02:13.353
Dira keeps account-specific commitments and private memory across sessions. Confirmed corrections can

00:02:13.353 --> 00:02:19.706
become reusable rules for later plans. You choose the connected tools, approval

00:02:19.706 --> 00:02:25.000
requirements, and messaging policy, and you can export your memory.

00:02:25.000 --> 00:02:29.286
The broker also blocks this forbidden destination and records the denial. These

00:02:29.286 --> 00:02:33.571
demo integrations are simulated; real Google checks are documented separately. OpenShell is

00:02:33.571 --> 00:02:37.857
not active around this hosted app. Dira’s goal is simple: help you

00:02:37.857 --> 00:02:40.000
keep the promises behind your calendar.
